IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s1-israeli-resident`
IMPORT `ito-s2-sources-of-income`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 1 ("Israeli resident" (a)) and s 2. Row IL-08.
-- Expected values from the text at lines 143-163 and 209-245; none edited to match the code.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — sections 1 and 2`

§§ `Section 1 — "Israeli resident"`

GIVEN `the year`      IS A NUMBER
      `days`          IS A NUMBER
      `three years`   IS A NUMBER
      `finding`       IS A MAYBE `Where the centre of life is`
      `rebutted`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident`
`in` `the year` `, days in Israel` `days` `, in three years` `three years` `, the finding` `finding` `, rebutted:` `rebutted` MEANS
    `An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident` WITH
        `tax year`                                                           IS `the year`
        `days in Israel in the tax year`                                     IS `days`
        `days in Israel in the tax year and the two tax years before it`     IS `three years`
        `the centre of life, as found on the whole of the individual's ties` IS `finding`
        `the presumption has been rebutted`                                  IS `rebutted`
        `regulations made under paragraph (4) reach the individual`          IS FALSE
        `section 14(b) reaches the individual in the tax year`               IS FALSE

-- (2)(a): 183 days or more. No finding, no rebuttal: presumed resident.
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 183 `, in three years` 183 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- 182 days and 400 over three years: no presumption, and no finding: declined, not "not resident".
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 182 `, in three years` 400 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE) BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
-- (2)(b): 30 days and 425 over three years.
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2) — a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises, for` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 30 `, in three years` 425 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 30 `, in three years` 425 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- 29 days, however many over three years: (b) fails, (a) fails.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2) — a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises, for` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 29 `, in three years` 900 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- 30 days and 424 over three years: (b) fails.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a)(2) — a presumption that the centre of life is in Israel arises, for` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 30 `, in three years` 424 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- (3): the presumption rebutted, and no finding recorded: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 200 `, in three years` 500 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` TRUE) BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
-- (1): a finding governs, whatever the days: abroad with 200 days, in Israel with 10.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 200 `, in three years` 500 `, the finding` (JUST `outside Israel`) `, rebutted:` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 10 `, in three years` 50 `, the finding` (JUST `in Israel`) `, rebutted:` FALSE)
-- A tax year before 2024.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`in` 2023 `, days in Israel` 365 `, in three years` 1095 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE) BECAUSE "row IL-08 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"
-- (4) and s 14(b), reached and not encoded.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident` WITH `tax year` IS 2026, `days in Israel in the tax year` IS 365, `days in Israel in the tax year and the two tax years before it` IS 1095, `the centre of life, as found on the whole of the individual's ties` IS NOTHING, `the presumption has been rebutted` IS FALSE, `regulations made under paragraph (4) reach the individual` IS TRUE, `section 14(b) reaches the individual in the tax year` IS FALSE) BECAUSE "the regulations under paragraph (4) of the definition of Israeli resident are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` (`An individual's year, for the definition of Israeli resident` WITH `tax year` IS 2026, `days in Israel in the tax year` IS 365, `days in Israel in the tax year and the two tax years before it` IS 1095, `the centre of life, as found on the whole of the individual's ties` IS NOTHING, `the presumption has been rebutted` IS FALSE, `regulations made under paragraph (4) reach the individual` IS FALSE, `section 14(b) reaches the individual in the tax year` IS TRUE) BECAUSE "section 14(b) displaces the definition of Israeli resident, and is not encoded in this model"

§§ `Section 2 — the charge, and work income`

`a salary paid abroad`       MEANS `An item of income, for section 2` WITH `source` IS `employment`, `produced or accrued in Israel` IS FALSE, `amount` IS 50
`a salary paid in Israel`    MEANS `An item of income, for section 2` WITH `source` IS `employment`, `produced or accrued in Israel` IS TRUE, `amount` IS 100
`a dividend from abroad`     MEANS `An item of income, for section 2` WITH `source` IS `dividend, interest, linkage differences or discount`, `produced or accrued in Israel` IS FALSE, `amount` IS 7

-- A resident is charged on income produced or accrued anywhere; a foreign resident only in Israel.
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `,` `a salary paid abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `s 2 — the item is within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `,` `a salary paid abroad`
#ASSERT `s 2 — the item is within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `,` `a salary paid in Israel`
#ASSERT `s 2 — the income within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` FALSE `, from` (LIST `a salary paid in Israel`, `a salary paid abroad`, `a dividend from abroad`) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `s 2 — the income within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `, from` (LIST `a salary paid in Israel`, `a salary paid abroad`, `a dividend from abroad`) EQUALS 157
-- s 1: work income is income under s 2(2).
#ASSERT `s 1 — work income:` `a salary paid abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — work income:` `a dividend from abroad`

§§ `Section 2A — declined (version 0.2.0, D035)`

-- Lottery winnings filed under s 2A: s 2A is not encoded, so neither the charge of s 2 nor the
-- income within it is answered. Work income is income under s 2(2), which these are not.
`lottery winnings in Israel` MEANS `An item of income, for section 2` WITH `source` IS `gambling, a lottery or a prize-bearing activity, under section 2A`, `produced or accrued in Israel` IS TRUE, `amount` IS 1000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2 — the item is within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `,` `lottery winnings in Israel` BECAUSE "section 2A (winnings from gambling, lotteries and prize-bearing activity) is not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2 — the income within the charge of section 2, for a person who is an Israeli resident:` TRUE `, from` (LIST `a salary paid in Israel`, `lottery winnings in Israel`) BECAUSE "section 2A (winnings from gambling, lotteries and prize-bearing activity) is not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — work income:` `lottery winnings in Israel`

§§ `Section 1 — the second limb of "foreign resident" (version 0.2.0, D019)`

GIVEN q            IS A NUMBER
      `outside`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `not centre` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A tax year of the individual, for the second limb of "foreign resident"`
`the facts of tax year` q `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` `outside` `; centre of life not in Israel:` `not centre` MEANS
    `A tax year of the individual, for the second limb of "foreign resident"` WITH
        `tax year`                                             IS q
        `outside Israel 183 days or more in the tax year`     IS `outside`
        `the centre of life was not in Israel in the tax year` IS `not centre`

-- An individual in 2026 with 100 days in Israel and a finding that his centre of life is in Israel:
-- resident under the definition of "Israeli resident" alone.
`H, 100 days in Israel in 2026, centre of life found in Israel` MEANS
    `in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 100 `, in three years` 300 `, the finding` (JUST `in Israel`) `, rebutted:` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 1 "Israeli resident" (a) — an Israeli resident in the tax year:` `H, 100 days in Israel in 2026, centre of life found in Israel`

-- The independent pass's D019: outside Israel 183 days or more in 2025 and 2026, centre of life in
-- Israel in those years and not in Israel in 2027 and 2028. The limb is met for the pair 2025-2026
-- (183 days out in each, centre of life not in Israel in 2027 and 2028): declined (fork F34).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — an Israeli resident in the tax year, the second limb of "foreign resident" considered:` `H, 100 days in Israel in 2026, centre of life found in Israel` `, the neighbouring tax years being` (LIST (`the facts of tax year` 2025 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE), (`the facts of tax year` 2026 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE), (`the facts of tax year` 2027 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` TRUE), (`the facts of tax year` 2028 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` TRUE)) BECAUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident is met for a pair of tax years that includes this one, and the text says neither which tax year it deems nor whether it prevails over a centre of life in Israel"
-- The pair 2026-2027 instead: outside 183 days in 2026 and 2027, centre of life not in Israel in 2028
-- and 2029, and in Israel 2025: declined (fork F34).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — an Israeli resident in the tax year, the second limb of "foreign resident" considered:` `H, 100 days in Israel in 2026, centre of life found in Israel` `, the neighbouring tax years being` (LIST (`the facts of tax year` 2025 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` FALSE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE), (`the facts of tax year` 2026 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE), (`the facts of tax year` 2027 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE), (`the facts of tax year` 2028 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` FALSE `; centre of life not in Israel:` TRUE), (`the facts of tax year` 2029 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` FALSE `; centre of life not in Israel:` TRUE)) BECAUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident is met for a pair of tax years that includes this one, and the text says neither which tax year it deems nor whether it prevails over a centre of life in Israel"
-- Only 2026's facts given, outside 183 days: neither pair is settled (2025 and 2027 are not given):
-- declined for want of the facts.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — an Israeli resident in the tax year, the second limb of "foreign resident" considered:` `H, 100 days in Israel in 2026, centre of life found in Israel` `, the neighbouring tax years being` (LIST (`the facts of tax year` 2026 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE)) BECAUSE "the second limb of the definition of foreign resident turns on the days outside Israel and the centre of life in the neighbouring tax years, and the facts given do not settle it"
-- Not outside 183 days in 2025 or in 2027: both pairs fail limb (a); resident.
#ASSERT `s 1 — an Israeli resident in the tax year, the second limb of "foreign resident" considered:` `H, 100 days in Israel in 2026, centre of life found in Israel` `, the neighbouring tax years being` (LIST (`the facts of tax year` 2025 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` FALSE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE), (`the facts of tax year` 2026 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE), (`the facts of tax year` 2027 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` FALSE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE))
-- Not outside 183 days in 2026 itself: both pairs fail; 2026 alone settles it; resident.
#ASSERT `s 1 — an Israeli resident in the tax year, the second limb of "foreign resident" considered:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 300 `, in three years` 900 `, the finding` (JUST `in Israel`) `, rebutted:` FALSE) `, the neighbouring tax years being` (LIST (`the facts of tax year` 2026 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` FALSE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE))
-- Not resident on the finding: the limb only agrees; FALSE whatever it shows.
#ASSERT NOT `s 1 — an Israeli resident in the tax year, the second limb of "foreign resident" considered:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 100 `, in three years` 300 `, the finding` (JUST `outside Israel`) `, rebutted:` FALSE) `, the neighbouring tax years being` (LIST (`the facts of tax year` 2025 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` TRUE), (`the facts of tax year` 2026 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` TRUE), (`the facts of tax year` 2027 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` TRUE), (`the facts of tax year` 2028 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` TRUE `; centre of life not in Israel:` TRUE))
-- No finding and no presumption: the first definition declines (fork F26), and so does this form.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 1 — an Israeli resident in the tax year, the second limb of "foreign resident" considered:` (`in` 2026 `, days in Israel` 100 `, in three years` 300 `, the finding` NOTHING `, rebutted:` FALSE) `, the neighbouring tax years being` (LIST (`the facts of tax year` 2026 `; outside Israel 183 days or more:` FALSE `; centre of life not in Israel:` FALSE)) BECAUSE "no finding of the centre of life has been made, and no unrebutted presumption decides it"
